HTML,
        'description_html' => <<<'HTML'
<p>Converting numbers to words (<strong>Convertidor de números a letras</strong>) is something many people need, yet Excel still has no function that does it easily, so a user-defined function is needed to achieve it.</p>
<h2>Number-to-words converter function in Excel</h2>
<p>I named the function I created to <strong>convert numbers to words in Excel</strong> CONVERTIRNUM, and its syntax is very simple:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Número</strong> (<em>Required</em>): the number you want to convert to words.</li>
<li><strong>CentimosEnLetra</strong> (<em>Optional</em>): indicates whether you want the cents (decimals) written out in words. If you enter FALSE (FALSO) or simply leave it out, the function shows the cents as a numeric value.</li>
<li><strong>Moneda</strong>: (<em>Required</em>) the name of your preferred currency in singular.</li>
<li><strong>Monedas: </strong>(<em>Required</em>) the name of your preferred currency in plural.</li>
</ul>
<p><img src="https://blogedwinortiznet.s3.amazonaws.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/07/24141326/8-1.jpg" alt="Number-to-words converter in Excel" width="528" height="314" srcset="https://blogedwinortiznet.s3.amazonaws.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/07/24141326/8-1-300x178.jpg 300w, https://blogedwinortiznet.s3.amazonaws.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/07/24141326/8-1.jpg 528w" sizes="(min-width: 760px) 720px, 100vw" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></p>
<p>It is worth stressing that you can use the <strong>number-to-words converter</strong> in combination with any other Excel function or formula, so you can convert all the text to uppercase, concatenate text, and so on.</p>
<p>You can also use this function in other projects, such as the <a href="/producto/factura-con-envio-por-correo-al-cliente/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Invoice with Email Delivery to the Customer</a> or any other workbook you use often.</p>
<h2></h2>
<h2>Additional considerations</h2>
<p>Please note that this function can <strong>convert numbers to words in Excel</strong> from zero up to 1,999,999,999. For any number outside this range, the function returns the message “ERROR: El número excede los límites” (the number exceeds the limits). Keep in mind that the function, its arguments and its messages are in Spanish.</p>
